KLEE is a symbolic virtual machine built on top of the LLVM compiler
infrastructure.  It executes LLVM bitcode modules with support for
symbolic values to automatically generate test cases that cover paths
through a program.

KLEE consists of two main components:

  * The core symbolic virtual machine engine, which runs LLVM bitcode
    while tracking symbolic values; and

  * A library for replaying computed test inputs on native code, plus a
    set of auxiliary tools (kleaver, ktest-tool, ktest-gen, ktest-randgen,
    klee-stats, klee-replay and klee-zesti).

Note that this build does not include the POSIX/uClibc runtime, since
uClibc is Linux-specific.  KLEE can therefore only execute closed
programs, i.e. programs that do not rely on an external C library.
